{"text": "Mark A. Davalos\n\nObjective\n\nEducation\n\nProfessional\nExperience\n\nMy career goal as an educator is to assist all youth in reaching their academic potential while\nbecoming lifelong learners directed at improving all quality of life. I truly believe that our\nschools can be the best part of our communities. Every parent and every student wants success\nand we must want the same. The school district is a huge part of how every child grows up and\nwe are given that honor each and every day to help build dreams into reality. I believe that all\nstudents can achieve and we must reduce learning gaps for those who struggle. I am a dedicated\nand lifelong educator who believes in public education and would offer knowledge, mentoring,\ndetermination, and vision towards helping others realize our educational vision.\n\nContinuing Administrator/ Initial Superintendent License; 2000-2005\nPortland State University, Portland, OR; Valid through 2015\n\nOregon Basic Administrative License; 1998-2000\nPortland State University, Portland, OR\n\nM Ed; Educational Management; 1993-1996\nUniversity of La Verne, La Verne, CA\n\nCA Preliminary Administrative Credential; 1996\nUniversity of La Verne, La Verne, CA\n\nB.A., Social Science; 1971-1975\nUniversity of La Verne, La Verne, CA\n\nSuperintendent; Saint Helens School District; Saint Helens, OR July 2011-Present\nSupervision of 6 Schools (All Grades K-12)\n* Hiring excellent teachers and leaders (Human Resource Management)\n+ Working collaboratively with teachers unions, communities and administrators (HRM)\n* Problem-solving high stress community situations (Communication Leader)\n* Equity and fairness in distribution of resources (Budget Management)\n* Providing support to developing leaders (Leadership)\n+ Systemic school improvement(Teaching & Learning Management)\n* Assisting low performing schools to increase student achievement\n* Removing barriers for students moving through the K-12 system to increase graduation rates\n\u00a2 Designing and implementing innovative programs based on best practices\n\nDeputy Superintendent; July 2009-July 2011; Portland Public School District, Portland, OR\nSupervision of 28 K-12 Schools in Region 2\n* Problem-solving high stress community situations\n+ Equity and fairness in distribution of resources\n* Providing support to developing leaders,\n+ Successful systemic school improvement, (AYP, Data Teams, PLC, RTI and Data Wise)\n\u00a2 Assisting low performing schools to increase student achievement\n* Removing barriers for students moving through the K-12 system\n+ Designing and implementing innovative programs\n* Hiring excellent leaders\n* Working collaboratively with teachers unions, communities and administrators\n+ Evaluate, Assign and Hire Administrators",
